			<div class="content" id="post-content-2407662">
									

<p>Thank you for the response. Letting an author know why you're downvoting something is probably one of the best things you can do.</p>
<p>In regards to your issues with the article, I originally had a set of three unnamed films that had effects that weren't behavioral altering at all. However, based on the responses I got to that (which were basically &quot;make it more interesting&quot;) I changed up the examples entirely and tried to be a bit more creative than just &quot;thing that gives you nausea&quot; &quot;thing that causes internal bleeding&quot; etc&#8230; Apparently, I either went too far in this or not far enough.</p>
<p>Do you feel it would be improved if I made one of them a non-behavioral altering one? Say, make the Toy Story one actually turn people into toys? (Just as a hypothetical example.)</p>

